{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"head up display head up display","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md","fileName":"Head-Up Display.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Head-Up Display","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-18 16:43\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Interface and Accessibility]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interface and Accessibility","Aiming Reticle","Game Radar Display","Waypoint Indicator","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"head up display head up display","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Head-Up Display.md","fileName":"Head-Up Display.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Head-Up Display","heading":"Head-Up Display","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A head-up display places indicators over the main view rather than in a separate screen area. It can show health, ammunition, objectives, maps, or other changing state while play continues.\n\nHUD elements should be readable against varied backgrounds and should not obscure the action they are meant to support. Information belongs there only when the player needs it frequently enough to justify persistent screen space.\n\nCommon programmable HUD elements include an [[Aiming Reticle]], [[Game Radar Display]], and [[Waypoint Indicator]]. Each converts game state or world-space information into stable screen-space feedback while the main scene continues to update.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interface and Accessibility","Aiming Reticle","Game Radar Disp